ly pass the >20-system hard block.\\nConditions:\\n1. feasibility-gate.md file location and Criterion 3 logic | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read tool confirmed file at plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md lines 28-32; Criterion 3 counts Impact Radius rows without any rg step\\n2. Impact Radius table schema (current column set) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep across plugins/development-harness for pattern: column confirmed none exists in any current Impact Radius table; backlog_core/operations.py and impact-analyst.md define the current schema\\n3. ripgrep invocation pattern for scope checking | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md lines 46-49 confirms rg -l '<pattern>' | wc -l is the canonical pattern; no existing usage in feasibility-gate.md confirmed by Grep\\n4. feasibility-gate execution model (AI instructions vs. code) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: feasibility-gate.md is skill reference documentation read by the AI agent during /dh:work-backlog-item workflow \u2014 not executed code\\n5. STALE_GROOM warning threshold | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Stated in item description \u2014 emit STALE_GROOM when live_count > 1.5 * manual_count\\n6. Downstream consumers of the Impact Radius row count | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep confirms feasibility-gate.md Criterion 3 is the sole consumer of the Impact Radius row count at gate time\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add ripgrep-based blast-radius enumeration to feasibility-gate impact radius scoring** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md \u2014 pattern: Transform Precision Definition (rg -l 'pattern' | wc -l for scope before planning)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-18)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 this is a feature item adding capability to existing AI-executed workflow instructions. No failure to reproduce.\\n\\nObservable symptom (documented in item): run /dh:work-backlog-item on a backlog item whose Impact Radius section was authored 2+ months ago. The feasibility gate fires Criterion 3 using the stale manual row count. There is no warning that the count is stale, no rg command is issued, and a high-blast-radius change proceeds without the correct count being checked against the >20-system threshold.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 \u2014 The missing guardrail is real and the symptom is concrete (stale counts silently passing the blast-radius hard block), but the >20-system threshold is rarely hit in practice and the workaround (manual re-groom before working a migration item) is straightforward. The risk is highest for long-lived backlog items on migration-class changes.\\n\\nEffort: Small \u2014 the primary change is a prose/instruction update to `feasibility-gate.md` adding an optional rg sub-step and STALE_GROOM warning, plus a schema documentation update in `impact-analyst.md`. No backlog_core code changes are required.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -c \\\"rg -l\\\" plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md` outputs at least 1 \u2014 the rg sub-step is present in the file\\n2. When the Impact Radius section of a backlog item contains a row with `pattern: 'some_pattern'`, running the feasibility gate workflow produces output containing `live_count: N (from rg)` alongside `manual_count: M`\\n3. When `live_count > 1.5 * manual_count`, the gate output contains the string `STALE_GROOM` and explicitly requires re-grooming before proceeding\\n4. When no `pattern:` field is present on any Impact Radius row, the gate behavior is identical to current behavior \u2014 no rg command is issued, no warning is emitted, Criterion 3 uses the manual row count as before (backward-compatible)\\n5. `impact-analyst.md` documents the optional `pattern:` column so grooming agents know they can include it for enumerable patterns\\n6. The PASS output contract in `feasibility-gate.md` is updated to include the new `live_count` / `manual_count` / `STALE_GROOM` fields when applicable\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill reference | `/dh:work-backlog-item` \u2014 feasibility-gate is part of this skill's work workflow |\\n| Agent | `@dh:impact-analyst` \u2014 defines Impact Radius table format; must gain `pattern:` column documentation |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md` \u2014 primary change target |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md` \u2014 secondary change target for pattern: column documentation |\\n| Research | `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md` \u2014 source of the `rg -l` pattern |\\n| Research | `research/insights/2026-05-10-composio-codebase-migrate-improvements.md` \u2014 improvement #4 origin record |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nDepends on: None \u2014 feasibility-gate.md is a standalone reference file; no other backlog item must be completed first.\\n\\nBlocks: None directly. #2241 (codemod-runner skill) would benefit from this item being complete \u2014 the codemod-runner skill would want Impact Radius rows to include `pattern:` fields so the feasibility gate can validate scope automatically before a large codemod runs.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe item's current state, target state, and measurable signal are internally consistent. The proposed change is additive and backward-compatible: the `pattern:` column is optional, so existing Impact Radius rows without it continue to work without modification. The STALE_GROOM warning does not alter the gate's pass/block decision \u2014 it surfaces information that enables a human or re-grooming step to correct the count before a high-blast-radius change proceeds unchecked. This matches the feasibility gate's design intent of answering \\\"should we do this and can it be done?\\\" with accurate, current information rather than stale groomed metadata.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: missing-guardrail\\n\\nRationale: The feasibility gate has a hard block at >20 systems but lacks the guard that validates the row count used to trigger that block. A gate that relies entirely on a human-authored static count is missing the automated validation step that would detect staleness. The gate exists, the threshold is correct, but the input to the gate is unvalidated against the live codebase state. This is a guardrail gap \u2014 the machinery for the decision is present but its input has no freshness guarantee.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| System | Role | Risk | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md` | producer | HIGH | Primary change surface \u2014 Criterion 3 block must gain the optional rg sub-step and STALE_GROOM warning logic |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md` | agent-instruction | MEDIUM | Defines the Impact Radius table format; the optional `pattern:` column must be documented here so grooming agents know to include it |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/scope.md` | documentation | MEDIUM | Documents that grooming must produce Impact Radius \u2014 may need a note that `pattern:` column is now optional |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` | documentation | LOW | Output validation gate checks for Impact Radius section presence \u2014 no change needed unless pattern: column becomes required |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` | documentation | LOW | References impact-analyst writing Impact Radius \u2014 may need mention of the pattern: column convention |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_impact_radius_conflicts.py` | test | LOW | Tests impact radius conflict detection, not feasibility gate logic \u2014 no direct change needed but a new test fixture may be added |\\n\\n**Total systems affected: 6**\\n**Blast radius category: 0\u201310 systems (within safe threshold)**\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md` uses Criterion 3 \\\"Blast radius\\\" by counting rows in the Impact Radius section (Code, Docs, Config, Agent Instructions). That count is produced manually during grooming \u2014 it is whatever the groomer wrote in the Impact Radius table at backlog item creation time.\\n\\nThere is no automated step that runs `rg -l '<pattern>' | wc -l` against the working tree to validate or refresh the row count before the feasibility gate fires. For migrations and renames that touch a \\\"find-all-uses\\\" pattern, the manually authored row count rapidly goes stale as the codebase evolves between grooming and execution.\\n\\nSymptom: feasibility-gate sees Impact Radius listing 8 systems based on a 2-month-old groom; the actual `rg` count today is 47, but the gate fires with the stale 8-count and never warns. A 47-system migration runs unscored against the >20 systems hard block at line 7-9 of `feasibility-gate.md`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`feasibility-gate.md` Criterion 3 has a new automated sub-step before the manual count: when the Impact Radius section contains an explicit `pattern: '<rg-pattern>'` field on a row, the gate runs `rg -l '<rg-pattern>' | wc -l` and uses the live count instead of (or in addition to) the manually-authored count. If live count > manual count by more than 50%, the gate emits a `STALE_GROOM` warning that requires re-grooming.\\n\\nThe Impact Radius table format (defined in the groomer's section template) gains an optional `pattern:` column for ripgrep-grep-able rows.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `grep -c \\\"rg -l\\\" plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md` \u2014 outputs at least 1.\\n\\nTest: groom a backlog item with an Impact Radius row containing `pattern: 'old_api_v1'`, then run feasibility-gate locally. Output shows `live_count: N (from rg)` alongside `manual_count: M`, and emits `STALE_GROOM` when N > 1.5 * M.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e8de0de1f31ddd9284e42c0a3fc7d01942298bfd41b1456cba2f4d04f46fcdb5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCQ-Jg\"}"}